    <main class="policy-container">
        <div class="policy-content">
            
            <section id="overview">
                <h2>1. Introduction & Core Philosophy</h2>
                <p>Welcome to <strong>WeatherGlow</strong> ("the App"), developed by <strong>NEURON TS LABS</strong>. We respect your privacy and are committed to protecting the device and environmental configuration details of our users.</p>
                <p>WeatherGlow is designed with a privacy-conscious architecture: we do not require account registration, login credentials, or personal identity profiles (such as your name, email, or phone number) to deliver accurate meteorological forecasts.</p>
                
                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <p><strong>Zero Continuous Tracking:</strong> WeatherGlow accesses your location strictly when triggered by user interaction or widget update cycles. The App does <strong>not</strong> track your physical location continuously in the background, nor do we construct movement history profiles on external servers.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="collection">
                <h2>2. Information We Collect & Process</h2>

                <h3>A. Location Data</h3>
                <p>WeatherGlow utilizes location parameters strictly to provide local atmospheric metrics:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Types of Data:</strong> Precise Location (<span class="code-inline">ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION</span>) and Coarse Location (<span class="code-inline">ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION</span>).</li>
                    <li><strong>Collection Triggers:</strong> Location is queried only when you tap the <strong>"Current GPS"</strong> action or enable location auto-detection during onboarding or in settings.</li>
                    <li><strong>Purpose & Geocoding:</strong> Coordinates (latitude and longitude) are converted on-device or through native Android geocoder APIs into area names (e.g., city, locality) to query real-time weather forecasts, air quality index (AQI) readings, UV indices, and solar cycles.</li>
                    <li><strong>Storage:</strong> Coordinates and saved city names reside strictly in your device's local database (<span class="code-inline">weather-glow.db</span>).</li>
                </ul>

                <h3>B. App Preferences & Cached Forecasts</h3>
                <p>Saved cities, default locations, temperature unit selections (Celsius/Fahrenheit), wind/pressure units, theme settings, and cached forecast payloads are saved <strong>locally on your device</strong> using Android DataStore and an on-device Room SQLite database. This data never leaves your device except to query external weather APIs for refreshed conditions.</p>

                <h3>C. Technical Identifiers & Diagnostics</h3>
                <p>Device specifications (model, OS version, screen resolution, locale), IP addresses, and the Google Advertising ID (GAID) are processed by standard network and advertising libraries to deliver localized weather responses, monitor technical errors, and display banners.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="permissions-matrix">
                <h2>3. System Permissions Transparency</h2>
                <p>WeatherGlow requests only the Android permissions necessary to support core forecast delivery and widget updates:</p>

                <table class="matrix-table">
                    <thead>
                        <tr>
                            <th>Permission</th>
                            <th>Category</th>
                            <th>Functional Purpose</th>
                        </tr>
                    </thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="code-inline">ACCESS_FINE_LOCATION</span></td>
                            <td>Location</td>
                            <td>Resolves high-accuracy GPS coordinates when tapping "Current GPS" to fetch local weather.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="code-inline">ACCESS_COARSE_LOCATION</span></td>
                            <td>Location</td>
                            <td>Determines approximate location via cellular/Wi-Fi networks for regional weather reports.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="code-inline">INTERNET</span></td>
                            <td>Network</td>
                            <td>Queries weather forecast endpoints, air quality metrics, and ad components.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="code-inline">ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</span></td>
                            <td>Network</td>
                            <td>Verifies network availability before dispatching weather synchronization requests.</td>
                        </tr>
                        <tr>
                            <td><span class="code-inline">RECEIVE_BOOT_COMPLETED</span></td>
                            <td>System</td>
                            <td>Restores and updates home screen widgets automatically following device reboots.</td>
                        </tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>

                <div class="highlight-box">
                    <p><strong>Background Location Policy:</strong> WeatherGlow intentionally does <strong>not</strong> request or declare <span class="code-inline">ACCESS_BACKGROUND_LOCATION</span>. Location queries occur only while the App is actively in use or during explicit user updates.</p>
                </div>
            </section>

            <section id="third-party">
                <h2>4. Third-Party Services & SDK Integrations</h2>
                <p>To deliver real-time atmospheric data and maintain the free version of the App, WeatherGlow interfaces with verified third-party partners:</p>

                <h3>A. OpenWeather API (Weather Service Provider)</h3>
                <p>Used to retrieve live weather conditions, hourly forecasts, 5-day forecasts, and air pollution measurements. Only geographical coordinates or searched locality query strings are transmitted to fetch accurate atmospheric data. For more details, consult the <a href="https://openweathermap.org/privacy-policy" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-cyan); text-decoration: none;">OpenWeather Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

                <h3>B. Google Play Services & Fused Location Provider</h3>
                <p>Utilized for battery-efficient location detection and reverse geocoding via standard Android system services. Handled under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-cyan); text-decoration: none;">Google Privacy Policy</a>.</p>

                <h3>C. Google Mobile Ads (AdMob)</h3>
                <p>Displays banner advertisements. AdMob may process advertising IDs, IP addresses, and interaction metrics to serve contextual or personalized advertisements in compliance with regional regulations. You can control or opt out of personalized ad targeting via <a href="https://adssettings.google.com/" target="_blank" style="color: var(--accent-cyan); text-decoration: none;">Google Ads Settings</a>.</p>
            </section>

            <section id="storage-security">
                <h2>5. Data Storage, Security & Retention</h2>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>No Remote User Account DB:</strong> NEURON TS LABS does not operate cloud databases holding user accounts, identities, or location tracking trails.</li>
                    <li><strong>Local Sandboxing:</strong> Saved cities and cached weather data reside locally within the application sandbox (<span class="code-inline">weather-glow.db</span>).</li>
                    <li><strong>Encrypted Transport:</strong> All remote calls to weather APIs and advertising platforms are enforced over secure HTTPS/TLS transport encryption.</li>
                    <li><strong>Retention:</strong> Local caches and preferences remain stored until you remove cities in-app, clear app storage, or uninstall the software.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="user-controls">
                <h2>6. Your Privacy Rights & Data Controls</h2>
                <p>You maintain full operational control over your data within WeatherGlow:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Revoking Location Permissions:</strong> You can revoke location access at any time via <em>Android Settings &gt; Apps &gt; WeatherGlow &gt; Permissions</em>. You can still manually search and save any city worldwide without location access.</li>
                    <li><strong>Managing Saved Cities:</strong> Delete specific cities or reset your default locations list at any time inside the <strong>Locations</strong> tab.</li>
                    <li><strong>Flushing Local Data:</strong> Clear all cached weather reports, settings, and databases via <em>Android Settings &gt; Apps &gt; WeatherGlow &gt; Storage &gt; Clear Data</em>.</li>
                    <li><strong>Advertising ID Reset:</strong> Reset or delete your device Advertising ID via <em>Android Settings &gt; Google &gt; Ads</em>.</li>
                </ul>
            </section>

            <section id="compliance">
                <h2>7. Children's Privacy & Regulatory Compliance</h2>
                <p>WeatherGlow is a general-audience weather utility and is not directed toward children under 13 years of age. We do not knowingly collect personal identifiable information from children.</p>
                <p>The App complies with international data frameworks, including the European General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) and California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA). We do not sell user personal data.</p>
            </section>

